# NEVER TRANSLATE LINE ENDINGS. NOT ON CHECKOUT, NOT ON COMMIT, NOT ON ANY PLATFORM.
#
# This is not a style preference. It is what makes the rest of the repository true.
#
# Git on Windows ships with `core.autocrlf=true` in its system config, and it was ON when
# this repository was created -- the first `git add` of the two published trees printed a
# CRLF warning for every text file in them. Left alone it would have done this:
#
#   * the blob stored in Git is LF, matching the published archive;
#   * every CHECKOUT rewrites it to CRLF;
#   * so a fresh clone -- CI, another machine, a reviewer's laptop -- gets a working tree
#     that does NOT byte-match the archive the trees were unpacked from.
#
# Three things this project depends on would then be quietly wrong, and none of them would
# announce it:
#
#   1. Branch 0's premise. It commits both published trees UNMODIFIED, and "unmodified" is
#      verified by SHA-256 against the archive. A CRLF checkout fails that comparison on
#      every text file while the diff shows nothing at all.
#   2. The byte-comparison harness. The pipeline's mechanical half is a deterministic
#      function and the test is to compare bytes. Line endings that vary by platform make
#      every such comparison meaningless.
#   3. The parity check. It compares the UK and US trees line by line. Two clones with
#      different checkout settings would disagree about trees that are in fact identical.
#
# A local `core.autocrlf=false` does not travel with a clone. This file does.
* -text

# Belt and braces for the two variant trees and the fixtures, so the intent survives anyone
# later relaxing the blanket rule above.
uk/**   -text
us/**   -text
tests/fixtures/**  -text -diff

# AND ONE EXCEPTION, ADDED 2026-09-02 WHEN THE FIRST *TEXT* FILE ARRIVED IN THAT DIRECTORY.
# The `-diff` above was written when `tests/fixtures/` held nothing but ZIP containers, where
# refusing to diff is simply correct. A fixture may now ship its OWN NOTES beside it -- the
# `paragraphs.json` a driving tool would otherwise invent -- and that file is the fixture's
# INPUT: a reviewer who cannot read it cannot review what the test asserts. So restore `diff`
# and KEEP `-text`, because the reason the blanket rule exists is unchanged: these bytes must
# never be retranslated on checkout, on any platform.
tests/fixtures/*.notes.json  -text diff

# Word documents and packaged skills are ZIP containers: binary, never diffed, never merged.
*.docx  binary
*.doc   binary
*.dotx  binary
*.skill binary
